npm (see package.json / package-lock.json in each workspace for the full,
exact list and versions). This section highlights the key direct
dependencies and their licenses, as recorded in each package's own
package.json at the time of writing:

  React, React DOM, React Router DOM .......... MIT
  Vite, @vitejs/plugin-react .................. MIT
  Tailwind CSS, @tailwindcss/vite ............. MIT
  Vitest, @testing-library/* ................... MIT
  Lucide React (icons) ......................... ISC
  Express ....................................... MIT
  Multer ........................................ MIT
  adm-zip ....................................... MIT
  Zod ........................................... MIT
  cors ........................................... MIT
  supertest ..................................... MIT

Each of these projects retains its own copyright and license. No
modified copies of their source code are redistributed as part of this
repository; they are consumed as standard npm dependencies.

================================================================================
AI model
================================================================================

RepoMedic AI's optional local AI layer is designed to work with models
served through Ollama (https://ollama.com) running on your own machine.
The default configured model, qwen2.5:1.5b (Qwen2.5, by Alibaba Cloud),
is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0, as published on its
Ollama library page (https://ollama.com/library/qwen2.5:1.5b) at the time
of writing. No model weights are bundled with, or distributed by, this
repository — they are downloaded directly from Ollama's model library by
the person running RepoMedic AI, under that model's own license.

See docs/ai-model.md for full detail, including what was and wasn't
independently verified.

